5. Financial Feasibility
In this section, we investigate whether the proposed system can be implemented and run for a reasonable cost. Two scenarios will be considered. First, the student prototype to be developed during the semester. Second, a small-scale university pilot, running for one year.
The cash cost of the prototype should be relatively low as the team members have laptops available to them with Internet connectivity. GitHub Free can be used to host private repositories at no cost per month [6]. Supabase Free can also be used for the prototype, as it allows for a 500 MB database and 1 GB of file storage at the moment [7]. This should be enough to hold the sample data needed for the project.
The team can be expected to use open-source or university-hosted software wherever possible. Some budget will be left for experimenting with external AI, e.g., the cost of the text-embedding-3-small model is listed at USD 0.02 per one million tokens [8]. This would make the cost of conducting simple semantic-matching experiments relatively low; however, a spending ceiling will still be imposed, as the natural-language assistant and AI report generation might involve extra costs in terms of API calls.
All figures in this section are given in dirhams. The figures in US dollars were converted using the exchange rate of USD 1 = AED 3.6725, published by the Central Bank of the UAE [6].

